## Protobuf Specification Evidence

The normative `SendMessageResponse` in `specification/grpc/a2a.proto` uses `oneof`:

```protobuf
message SendMessageResponse {
  oneof response {
    Task task = 1;
    Message message = 2;
  }
}
```

Per [Protobuf JSON Mapping](https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/proto3/#json):
> For a oneof field, the serialized form is the serialized form of the field with value. Only one of the fields (the field with value) is serialized.

Result: **Only one field is serialized in JSON, using that field's name as key**.

```json
// Correct (wrapped):
{"task": {...}}

// Correct (wrapped):
{"message": {...}}

// Incorrect (direct format does NOT match proto semantics):
{"id": "...", "kind": "task", ...}
```

## Recommendation: Adopt Option 1 (Wrapped Format)

